<h1>About le website</h1>

<p>The Autredex (fr: other-dex) is a semi-private media archive and experimental imageboard project primarily maintained by <a href="https://www.arctaxia.ink/">Arctaxia</a>.</p>

<p>The goal of this website is to organize, document, and archive the highest-quality media related to Alcest and anything related as possible.</p>

<h2>Questions you might have.</h2>

<ol>
    <li><strong>Are you, or this website, associated with the band Alcest, or their managers/labels/etc-etc</strong></li>

    <p><em>NO</em>. I am a loser living in a deadbeat city in california, that makes crappy alcest-themed websites on my failing laptop for the heck of it.</p>

    <li><strong>Why is the site closed off? And why can&#39;t I register for an account?</strong></li>

    <p>The site is invite only for several reasons.</p>
    <p>For one, it&#39;s a hobby project that I made (besides simply for fun) to learn web development and system administration, and I don&#39;t want it being scraped or overpublicized by search engines or generative AI (large language models, scraping efforts for image generator training, etc.), and second, limiting the userbase makes things much easier for me to manage (and moderate). </p>
    <p>If you really want an account, contact me on Discord for one. I&#39;ll be more likely to give you an account if I&#39;m familiar with you or you&#39;ve been a active member of the alcest discord server for a while.</p>

    <li><strong>Why would you do this?</strong></li>

    <p>Because:</p>
    <ul>
    <li>it&#39;s fun </li>
    <li>I need someplace to properly organize all those random pictures I saved</li>
    <li>Alcest will clear their instagram when a new album releases</li>
    <li>Pinterest is enshittified Dog Booty</li>
    </ul><br>

    <li><strong>Why are you banning NSFW?</strong></li>

    <p>I am NOT a &quot;prude&quot;, &quot;puritan&quot;, whatever word you want to use, but the main topic of this website heavily involves <em>real people</em> and I don&#39;t want to be held liable for hosting that sort of content once any <em>real people</em> involved start complaining. There are other places where you can post that stuff</p>

    <li><strong>The color themes are pretty (or ugly), what inspired them?</strong></li>

    <p>The colors are inspired by the themes used on alcest&#39;s myspace profile and website during the late 2000s to early 2010s. </p>
